From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1q9lugp <lackowork84@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:25:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/34] v3d: 3.3 register allocation keeps spill candidates for
 1 thread

On 3.3 a shader that doesn't allocate is retried in the same compile
at 4, 2 and 1 threads, and 0001 allows TMU spills only at 1 thread.
v3d_choose_spill_node marked the temps it couldn't spill by clearing
them in c->spillable, which outlives the attempt: after the 2-thread
round no TMU-spillable temp was left, the 1-thread round found no spill
candidate (2188 temps, 0 spills) and the shader failed with every
strategy, so the draw was skipped (GLES3
texture.units.all_units.only_cube.{1,2,7}: 24 cube lookups, the image
kept the clear colour). Keep "can't spill in this attempt" local; the
shader now compiles at 1 thread with 2 spills.
---
 src/broadcom/compiler/vir_register_allocate.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_register_allocate.c b/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_register_allocate.c
index 5879de1..337e199 100644
--- a/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_register_allocate.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_register_allocate.c
@@ -274,11 +274,17 @@ v3d_choose_spill_node(struct v3d_compile *c)
         const float tmu_scale = 10;
         float block_scale = 1.0;
         float spill_costs[c->num_temps];
+        /* TMU spills not possible in this attempt.  Kept out of
+         * c->spillable: a retry at fewer threads can spill them.
+         */
+        bool no_tmu_spill[c->num_temps];
         bool in_tmu_operation = false;
         bool started_last_seg = false;
 
-        for (unsigned i = 0; i < c->num_temps; i++)
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < c->num_temps; i++) {
                 spill_costs[i] = 0.0;
+                no_tmu_spill[i] = false;
+        }
 
         /* XXX: Scale the cost up when inside of a loop. */
         vir_for_each_block(block, c) {
@@ -313,7 +319,7 @@ v3d_choose_spill_node(struct v3d_compile *c)
                                                               tmu_scale *
                                                               tmu_op_scale);
                                 } else {
-                                        BITSET_CLEAR(c->spillable, temp);
+                                        no_tmu_spill[temp] = true;
                                 }
                         }
 
@@ -328,7 +334,7 @@ v3d_choose_spill_node(struct v3d_compile *c)
                                         spill_costs[temp] += (block_scale *
                                                               tmu_scale);
                                 } else {
-                                        BITSET_CLEAR(c->spillable, temp);
+                                        no_tmu_spill[temp] = true;
                                 }
                         }
 
@@ -364,6 +370,7 @@ v3d_choose_spill_node(struct v3d_compile *c)
         for (unsigned i = 0; i < c->num_temps; i++) {
                 if (BITSET_TEST(c->spillable, i)) {
                         ra_set_node_spill_cost(c->g, temp_to_node(c, i),
+                                               no_tmu_spill[i] ? 0.0 :
                                                spill_costs[i]);
                 }
         }
